{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1472 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "220936a57e5d3bcf2113e276710b78af83938f8842f3b0670cbec815fdfceb1d" :edb/db-before-t 1471 :edb/db-after-t 1472 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534784 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:48:12.728Z" 13194139534784 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310017 13194139534784 true] [17592186100731 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310024 13194139534784 true] [17592186101359 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534784 true] [17592186101359 1100 "What is the value of ${\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534784 true] [17592186101359 1100 "What is the value of $∫_{e^{2}}^{e^{4}}\\frac{8\\ln x}{x}dx$?" 13194139534784 false] [17592186101359 1145 "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$  gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | ${e}^{2}$ | ${e}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =8{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =8\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {u}^{2}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (16-4) \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310018 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1089 "q-13841" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1100 "What is the value of ${\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1113 #uuid "0a679363-232d-5c04-b893-cdbd8f524a7d" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310017 1145 "Let's set $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x).$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2x}\\cdot 2=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $e/2$ | ${e}^{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{2}{3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{e/2}^{{e}^{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310019 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310020 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310021 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310022 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310023 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1041 "selection" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310020 13194139534784 true] [17592186310018 1110 #uuid "bf86d338-fd0a-56c1-b35f-596c3fe60672" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310019 1034 "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534784 true] [17592186310019 1111 #uuid "bb012fcb-41af-5561-8d79-10763e8c68cd" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310020 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534784 true] [17592186310020 1111 #uuid "dc0cb86b-1487-5387-bfb3-d08d26c8bd1f" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310021 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139534784 true] [17592186310021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534784 true] [17592186310021 1111 #uuid "dbac174e-c797-56ba-85de-c69ec